        "text": "Para decir que algo NO ES o NO ESTÁ, solo tenemos que agregar la palabra NOT después de am, is o are. ¡Es muy fácil!",
        "sections": [
          {
            "title": "Negar con I (yo)",
            "text": "I + am + not = I am not. Esta forma NO se puede acortar. Siempre se dice completo.",
            "examples": [
              "I am not a doctor.",
              "I am not tired.",
              "I am not at home."
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Negar con He / She / It",
            "text": "is + not se puede acortar a isn't. Las dos formas son correctas.",
            "examples": [
              "He is not at school. = He isn't at school.",
              "She is not sad. = She isn't sad.",
              "It is not Monday. = It isn't Monday."
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Negar con You / We / They",
            "text": "are + not se puede acortar a aren't. Las dos formas son correctas.",
            "examples": [
              "You are not late. = You aren't late.",
              "We are not at home. = We aren't at home.",
              "They are not from Germany. = They aren't from Germany."
            ]
          }
